  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently the FeSL relationship resolver makes use of the API-M relationships methods to query an object;s relationships (eg when determining hierarchical resource id and in the resource index attribute finder).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If the resource index module is enabled, the resolver should instead use the resource index directly.  This will enable more flexibility in defining how hierarchical resource identifiers should be formed, and will allow greater flexibility in the resource index attribute finder.  Currently there is a restriction that the relationships need to be in the object that is the XACML resource.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Note that this should fall back to using the API-M methods if the RI is disabled, so that FeSL is not dependent on the RI.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
